          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The HTML paragraph element defines a paragraph. Paragraphs are used to structure a text. A paragraph always starts on a new line, and browsers automatically add some white space (a ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "AbOSsxIGAkVSMh1dhVbK4",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "margin",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ") before and after a paragraph.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Breaking up content into paragraphs helps to make a page more accessible. Screen-readers and other assistive technology provide shortcuts to let their users skip to the next or previous paragraph, letting them skim content like how white space lets visual users skip around.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
